      <Card title="2. Utility Computing & ASP" badge="2000s" glow="cyan">
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 font-bold mb-1">Computing packaged like water and electricity.</p>
        <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-900 font-medium">
          Application Service Providers (ASPs) hosted single-tenant applications. Utility computing introduced metered billing, treating CPU cycles and gigabytes as consumable public commodities.
        </p>
      </Card>

      <Card title="3. Virtualization & Cloud" badge="2006–Present" glow="amber">
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 font-bold mb-1">Hardware hypervisors enable dynamic multi-tenant clouds.</p>
        <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-900 font-medium">
          Hardware virtualization (x86 hypervisors) decoupled operating systems from physical silicon. Combined with self-service REST APIs, Amazon launched EC2 and S3 in 2006, creating modern cloud computing.
        </p>
      </Card>
