        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-900 font-medium">
          Cloud computing fundamentally transforms corporate IT finance by converting <strong>Capital Expenditures (CAPEX)</strong> into <strong>Operational Expenditures (OPEX)</strong>.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs">
          <div class="lecture-card border-2 border-slate-300">
            <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-indigo-900 mb-1">CAPEX (On-Premises)</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-1 pl-4 list-disc text-slate-900 font-medium">
              <li>Buying physical servers, switches, SAN storage.</li>
              <li>Datacenter land purchase or long-term lease.</li>
              <li>HVAC power, backup diesel generators, UPS.</li>
              <li>3–5 year fixed depreciation cycles.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="lecture-card border-2 border-slate-300">
            <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-indigo-900 mb-1">OPEX (Cloud Utility)</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-1 pl-4 list-disc text-slate-900 font-medium">
              <li>Zero upfront hardware purchase.</li>
              <li>Pay per second of CPU and gigabyte-month storage.</li>
              <li>Fully tax-deductible operational expense.</li>
              <li>Scale down capacity instantly to stop billing.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 font-medium m-0">
          <strong>TCO Invariant:</strong> Total Cost of Ownership includes hardware, electricity, cooling, physical security guards, and system administrator salaries.
        </p>
      </div>

