        <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-900 font-medium">
          Laws like the European Union's GDPR, US HIPAA, and national banking acts mandate that citizen data must not leave physical geographical borders. Multi-cloud data replication must enforce geo-fencing restrictions.
        </p>
      </Card>

      <Card title="Cloud Financial Engineering (FinOps)" badge="Cost Control" glow="cyan">
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 font-bold mb-1">Managing dynamic, variable cloud spend at enterprise scale.</p>
        <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-900 font-medium">
          Without automated governance, developer-provisioned instances, unattached EBS volumes, and oversized clusters create massive financial waste. FinOps combines tagging, rightsizing, and reserved instances.
        </p>
      </Card>

      <Card title="Identity & Security Governance" badge="Zero Trust" glow="amber">
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 font-bold mb-1">The perimeter-less security model.</p>
        <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-900 font-medium">
          Traditional corporate firewalls no longer apply. Microservices communicate across public networks, requiring Zero-Trust security: mutual TLS (mTLS), short-lived IAM tokens, and least-privilege role policies.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </div>
    <SpeakerNotes>
      Explain Zero Trust: "Never trust, always verify." Every service call must authenticate and authorize even inside private subnets.
    </SpeakerNotes>
